{
  "abstract": "Finite quadratic-jet determinant estimates need one approximation space for many node radii and selected derivative columns. Building on the accepted Paper48/v1 circular-Jacobi comparison, we develop a cumulative consumer that uses several rank-dependent native spaces on one ordered charge spectrum without assuming that the spaces are nested. Each disjoint spectral interval receives one tail estimate, while all remaining eigenvalues are paid in aggregate. At the unchanged imported source, the frozen rank grid gives normalized correction greater than $0.0101156964790106081$. An explicit entropy modulus transports this profile to every positive integer scale under unchanged normalized geometry, capacities and original square-selection hypotheses. We also prove joint concavity of the finite circular-Jacobi entropy and derive closed tangent planes. With a fixed center on each rank interval, the source rate is affine in charge and rank; exact polygon vertices therefore certify complete rank families. Of 120 prescribed families, 119 pass and one omitted design receives no credit. The families alone give correction greater than $0.0101997722949777898$, and their ordered spectral maximum with the grid gives greater than $0.0104230524050248947$. Conditional integer-scale correction is greater than $0.0104230345217631738$. The imported source arithmetic and uncredited gap are unchanged; no new arithmetic rank, discriminant endpoint, census or classification is claimed. The imported $D\\leq498$ consequence retains its separate $D\\leq499$ theorem qualification. Author controls and clean CPU replays support the certificates, while independent mathematical assessment of the new geometric covers remains outstanding.",
